message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, my face and neck have been swelling up over the last three days. It’s really tender, and I can’t lie flat because I feel short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had fevers up to 102. But I can swallow fine. Just drooling a bit at night, which is weird."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We did a CT scan and it shows your parotid glands are enlarged on both sides, but no abscess. ENT thinks it’s sialadenitis—swelling of the salivary glands."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I couldn’t breathe well after the CT scan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s why we’re admitting you to the ICU tonight. We’re concerned about airway swelling. You got steroids and epinephrine, which helped. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My leg wound is okay, but it’s oozing a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2177-12-25 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have wound care look at it. For now, we’re focused on your neck. Your white count is up and lactate is elevated, so we started antibiotics just in case there’s infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2177-12-26 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through the night without any breathing issues. That’s a big relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2177-12-26 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I feel a bit better. Still swollen, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2177-12-26 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending tests for viruses like mumps, EBV, and CMV. Your mumps IgG is positive, so you’ve had it before. IgM is pending—could mean a reactivation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2177-12-26 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought I was vaccinated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2177-12-26 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were, but immunity can wane. We’re also checking for fungal and bacterial causes. We’ll keep you on IV antibiotics for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2177-12-26 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back negative. No bacteria growing. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2177-12-26 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2177-12-26 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not a bloodstream one. But your parotid glands are still inflamed. ENT and Infectious Disease think it could be viral or related to your psoriatic arthritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2177-12-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EBV and CMV tests came back negative. No sign of those viruses. Mumps IgM is still pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2177-12-27 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the rash on my chest? It showed up after the IV steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2177-12-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Dermatology saw you. They think it’s pustular psoriasis, which can flare after high-dose steroids. We’re starting a strong topical cream—clobetasol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2177-12-27 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that go away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2177-12-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it should improve. We’ll keep the cream going until your dermatology follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2177-12-27 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to transfer you to the regular floor today. Your breathing is stable, and you’re off oxygen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2177-12-27 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can I use my CPAP again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2177-12-27 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Your face is still too swollen. We’ll try it later. For now, we’ll monitor you at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2177-12-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your INR was high when you came in—4.8—so we held your warfarin. It’s now 1.7, so we restarted it at a higher dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2177-12-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take 6 mg at home. Why the change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2177-12-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started at 10 mg to get you therapeutic faster, but we’ll adjust based on tomorrow’s INR. Goal is around 2 to 3."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2177-12-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re placing a PICC line so you can get IV antibiotics at home if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2177-12-28 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2177-12-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s standard. We’ll make sure it’s positioned correctly with a chest X-ray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2177-12-28 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray showed the PICC tip was too far—it was in the right atrium. We pulled it back. Now it’s in the right spot in the SVC."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2177-12-28 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2177-12-28 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Could be, long-term. But we caught it quickly. You’re fine now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2177-12-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your skin scraping showed Trichophyton—fungal infection, probably ringworm on your arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2177-12-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know I had that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2177-12-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common. We’ll keep the antifungal cream you’re already on—miconazole. It should clear up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2177-12-29 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lactate is normal now—down from 5. That means your body is handling oxygen better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2177-12-29 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was that from the infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2177-12-29 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. But you never had a fever, so we think it was from inflammation. It’s improving with treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2177-12-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.7—perfect. We’re lowering your warfarin to 4 mg daily, which is less than your home dose, but safer for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2177-12-30 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll check it at home and call my doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2177-12-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. Also, we’re switching you from IV to oral antibiotics—just a precaution."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2177-12-30 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "ENT re-evaluated you. They don’t think this is a bacterial infection. More likely inflammation from your psoriatic arthritis or a viral cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2177-12-30 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2177-12-30 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started them because we couldn’t rule out infection. But now that you’re improving, we’ll stop them soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2177-12-31 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Swelling is less, and your labs are stable. We’re stopping the IV antibiotics today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2177-12-31 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2177-12-31 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly by tomorrow. We want to make sure your INR stays stable and you’re eating and breathing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2177-12-31 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started you on Bactrim daily. Since you’re on chronic steroids, you need protection against a lung infection called PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2177-12-31 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken that before. Is it necessary?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2177-12-31 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, ID recommends it. Steroids lower your immunity, so this is a safety measure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2178-01-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your mumps IgM came back pending—still no result. Until we know, avoid kids, pregnant women, and anyone with cystic fibrosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2178-01-01 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My family is vaccinated. Should I still worry?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2178-01-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Better safe. We’ll follow up with the state lab. For now, just be cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2178-01-01 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging you tomorrow. You’re breathing well, swelling is down, and labs are good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2178-01-01 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my leg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2178-01-01 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wound care says it’s healing. Keep it clean and watch for redness or increased drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Here’s your discharge summary. Follow up with ID, ENT, and your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if you have trouble breathing, fever, or the rash worsens. And get those outpatient labs done—LDH and liver tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Have a good one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep using your CPAP as tolerated. Even if it’s uncomfortable, try to use it part of the night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’ll build up slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And keep checking your INR. Call your doctor with the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve got a home monitor. I’ll stay on top of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. That helps a lot. Any other questions before you leave?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m good. Everything’s clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Take it easy, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we like to hear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our pleasure. Rest up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2178-01-02 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2177-12-25 20:02:00",
    "admission_end": "2178-01-02 21:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with a history of psoriatic arthritis, insulin-dependent diabetes, morbid obesity, and recent MSSA cellulitis was admitted for bilateral neck swelling and facial edema causing shortness of breath. Initially admitted to the ICU for airway monitoring, he received IV dexamethasone and racemic epinephrine after developing respiratory distress during imaging. CT showed symmetrically enlarged parotid glands without abscess, consistent with sialadenitis. He was treated with IV clindamycin for possible bacterial superinfection, later discontinued as ENT and infectious disease concluded the inflammation was likely viral or related to his underlying psoriatic arthritis. A new pustular psoriasis rash on the chest and arms, triggered by steroid use, was managed with clobetasol. A fungal infection (tinea corporis) on the forearm was identified and treated with miconazole. His warfarin was held due to an INR of 4.8, then restarted and titrated to 4 mg daily with a therapeutic INR of 2.7 at discharge. He improved clinically, was weaned off IV therapy, and discharged home with outpatient follow-up and lab monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Sialoadenitis",
      "Chronic pulmonary embolism",
      "Cellulitis and abscess of neck",
      "Ulcer of other part of lower limb",
      "Psoriatic arthropathy",
      "Other fluid overload",
      "Dermatophytosis of the body",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants"
    ]
  }
}
